% Number 86. Chace vol. II pl. 109 (photograph XXXI), PDF pp. 265-266; Peet pp. 128-129 (Pl. Y).
% Not a computation: fragments of a memorandum of accounts pasted on the back of the papyrus as patches.
% Every line is broken at both ends. Words in red in Chace are in braces. Chace prints amounts in the
% hundred notation ('2 '4 10 5 = 90); the numbers are kept inside the quotes and not computed.
% Chace: "The last four lines of the original are mere repetitions of the preceding line and are ignored."
No. 86
"... living forever." {"Amount of the food"} "in Hebenty ..."
"... his brother the steward Ka-mose ..."
"... of year his;" {"silver 50 times 2 to a year ..."}
"... ox 2;" {"in silver 3 in a year ..."}
"... one times 2, namely (?)" {"'6 and '6."} "As for one ..."   % Chace: "'6 twice" here and at the end of No. 82B; "there is no evidence that '6 only was intended in either place"
"... hinu 12;" {"in silver '4"} "one hinu ..."
"... silver 5 price their therefor fish 120 times 2 ..."
"... year barley quadruple hekat '2 '4 10 5;" {"spelt 100 hekat ..."}   % = 90 (Peet: 90 quadruple-hekat of barley, 100 + x of spelt)
"... [year] barley [quadruple hekat] '2 '4 10 5;" {"spelt 100 hekat '2 '4 10 5 2 ..."}   % Peet: "90 of barley, 192 of spelt"
"... 146 '2; barley 100 hekat '2 '4 10;" {"spelt 300 hekat ..."}   % Peet: "146 '2 (?); 185 (?) of barley, 300 + x of spelt"
"... '2 was brought wine, donkey(-load) 1 ..."
"... silver '2 (?) 4; in silver ..."
"... 1 '4, fat hinu 36; in silver ..."
"... 100 hekat '2 '4 20 1;" {"spelt barley 400 hekat 10 ..."}   % = 196 and 410. Chace: Peet interchanged "spelt" and "barley" in his translation ("hundred and ninety-six ... of barley, 410 quadruple-hekat of spelt")
